  "body": "The `<template>` element provides an easy way for developers to stamp out repeated chunks of content:\r\n\r\n```html\r\n<template id=chunk>\r\n  <div>Duplicated content here</div>\r\n</template>\r\n<script>\r\n  // Add 100 copies of this chunk\r\n  for (var i = 0; i < 100; i++)\r\n    document.body.appendChild(chunk.content.cloneNode(true));\r\n</script>\r\n```\r\n\r\nBut as seen in the example above, **Javascript must be used** for the \"stamping\" operation. What if there were a declarative way to stamp out templates? Something like this:\r\n\r\n```html\r\n<template id=my-template>\r\n  <div>Duplicated content here</div>\r\n</template>\r\n\r\n<div clone=my-template></div>\r\n<div clone=my-template></div>\r\n<div clone=my-template></div>\r\n```\r\n\r\nHere, the `clone=my-template` attribute refers back to the pre-existing `<template>`, and stamps out a clone of that template in-place. The resulting DOM would look like this, for the above example:\r\n\r\n```html\r\n<template id=my-template>\r\n  <div>Duplicated content here</div>\r\n</template>\r\n\r\n<div clone=my-template>\r\n  <div>Duplicated content here</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div clone=my-template>\r\n  <div>Duplicated content here</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div clone=my-template>\r\n  <div>Duplicated content here</div>\r\n</div>\r\n```\r\n\r\nOf course, there are many questions, such as:\r\n 1. What happens if the original `<div clone=my-template>` contained children - do they get left in? Or ignored?\r\n 2. The usual idref type questions, like what happens if the `<template>` comes after the clone? And what if it's in another tree?\r\n 3. How might this work with the [DOM Part API](https://github.com/WICG/webcomponents/blob/gh-pages/proposals/DOM-Parts.md) (aka Template Instantiation)? \r\n 4. Bikeshedding the `clone` attribute name.\r\n\r\nThis seems like it would be useful for (at least) Server Side Rendering, to save bytes on repeated content. This also comes up repeatedly in the discussion of declarative Shadow DOM, but as I've [written here](https://github.com/mfreed7/declarative-shadow-dom/blob/master/README.md#isnt-it-tedious-to-repeat-the-contents-of-each-shadow-root), it would seem to be a general problem including repeated light-DOM HTML.\r\n\r\n(I looked around for another similar proposal, and didn't find anything. Forgive me if I missed it!)",
